  "id": "COMPOUND:23441 - PROTEIN:5829",
  "verbalization": "Corticatic Acid E is implicated in the regulation of CHP-134 through a series of molecular interactions involving dual serine/threonine and tyrosine protein kinases. This pathway is targeted by multiple compounds, including Ascidiathiazone B, Ergocryptine, and Npc115753, all of which ultimately lead to the activation of CHP-134. The shared target of these compounds suggests a potential mechanism by which Corticatic Acid E may influence CHP-134 through the modulation of these protein kinases. The evidence supports a role for Corticatic Acid E in modulating the activity of these kinases, which in turn may affect CHP-134. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible regulatory relationship where Corticatic Acid E could act as a modulator of the signaling cascade involving these kinases, potentially influencing CHP-134 through a complex network of interactions.",
